gascoigne is token optimizer for LLM agents. It sits between agent and agent
reads (shell output, MCP tool results, web pages), shrinks it, and keeps every original in
local ledger so nothing ever lost.

Output gascoigne already optimized (exec, MCP server, proxy) recognized by
hint and left alone, are gascoigne's own MCP tools. **Read** never replaced: Claude
numbers lines shows, and dropped lines would shift numbers. **WebSearch**
left too: results (a median 608 tokens in measured sessions) rendered Claude
Code from fixed structure.

Measured on 16 Claude Code sessions (3,148 tool results): tool result stays in context for
**median 110 later requests** (mean 145, deciles 17–335), and 0.8% of gaps between
requests exceed 5-minute cache TTL. So rereads, not first read, make up most
cost: on Opus 5.5 token saved is worth $5/MTok at first read and about $31/MTok in
context.

Most new support is a **dialect**: a new tool in a family gascoigne already has. A new
**optimizer** is only for a new family. Other component kinds (receivers, filters,
exporters, extensions) follow the same package shape.

Every run appears as it happens, with its savings, content type and, when it was not
optimized, the reason. Click a run to compare the original with what the agent read, side by
side, and see each optimizer's step.

Ids first 8 hex digits text's sha256 (12, 16 or 64 when prefix holds a
different text), so same output from any session stored once and its hint costs ~7
fewer tokens. Originals gzip-compressed. Source keys longer 200 bytes (whole
command lines, heredocs) stored as 160-byte prefix plus hash. Ledgers older
versions converted on first open and vacuumed (a real one: 22 MB → 6 MB).

One self-contained page served from the binary, with no external requests. It follows the
system's light or dark theme; the *Auto / Light / Dark* switch in the header overrides it
and is remembered per browser.

run that lost over 99.5% large output gets warning to check it. optimized text
is kept next original (gzip, same retention), so runs recorded before show only
original. Viewing either here does not mark source failing.
